# Cost-aware subagent routing

- Use `composer-2.5-fast` for bounded subagent work whenever it can reliably
  inspect, test, verify, research, or summarize independently.
- Keep the primary agent responsible for scope, scientific or architectural
  decisions, destructive actions, commits, merges, deployments, and final
  synthesis.
- Do not delegate trivial one-step work or create redundant agents; delegation
  should reduce expensive primary-model turns, not multiply calls.
- Give each subagent a narrow prompt, exact repository/worktree, read/write
  limits, expected evidence, and a concise return format.
- Prefer one well-scoped Composer agent over repeated polling or open-ended
  retry loops. Reuse or resume an agent only when its retained context helps.
- Run independent checks in parallel when that lowers elapsed time without
  duplicating work.
